Check_activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs_V2
    [Documentation]    Check "activated successfully at airphone" on egate console Logs
    ...                to validate we need almost only ${occurency} answers and if answers need to be seen on the
    ...                the same milisec or not
    ...
    ...  Users of this KW :
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!
    ...  ! Test                 !  activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs  ! need 2 know if occ are in the same milisecond!
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!
    ...  ! TC 2640-AB_04 SA     !  this TC check only if present at least one time !  no                                          !
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!
    ...  ! TC 8533-AB401 Step1  !  this TC check if there is 0 occurency           !  no                                          !
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!
    ...  ! TC 8533-AB401 Step2  !  this TC check if there is 2 occurency           !  in the same millisec                        !
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!
    ...  ! TC 8533-AB401 Step3  !  this TC check if there is 3 occurency           !  if the 2 first are in the same millisec     !
    ...  !                      !                                                  !  if the 2 last  are in different millisec    !
    ...  !======================+==================================================+==============================================!

    [Arguments]    ${occurency}=1    ${samemilisecond}=${none}    ${deviation}=0
    # ajout deviation
    Dated log   Check_activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs_V2 arguments: >${occurency}< >${samemilisecond}< >${deviation}<
    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${pattern}=      set variable    activated successfully at airphone
    Dated log    pattern: ${pattern}
    ${output}        SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...              command=grep "${pattern}" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
    ...              host=${HOST_EPCSIM}
    Dated log    output:  ${output}

    Should Not Be Empty             ${output}
    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${output}        SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...              command=grep "${pattern}" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
    ...              host=${HOST_EPCSIM}

    Dated log       === check res answer ===
    Dated log       res answer:  ${output}

    Run keyword if    '${occurency}'=='0'    Fail    we find an occurency on this period

    ${dod}=    Run keyword if    '${occurency}'=='2'    subCheckmilisec_V2    samemilisecond=${samemilisecond}    between_occ=1-2
    ...                                                                       deviation=${deviation}
    ${dod}=    Run keyword if    '${occurency}'=='3'    subCheckmilisec_V2    samemilisecond=${samemilisecond}    between_occ=2-3
    ...                                                                       deviation=${deviation}
    #${occurency}'=='0' is TC AB04 case
    Run keyword if    '${occurency}'=='0'and'${dod}'=='${false}'    Fail    check if occurency are on same millisec fail

Check_activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs
    [Documentation]    Check "activated successfully at airphone" on egate console Logs
    ...                to validate we need almost 1 only answer. If 2 answers are present they need to not be
    ...                at the same milisec
    ...
    [Arguments]    ${samemilisecond}=${none}
    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${pattern}=      set variable    activated successfully at airphone
    Dated log    pattern: ${pattern}
    ${output}        SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...              command=grep "${pattern}" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
    ...              host=${HOST_EPCSIM}
    Dated log    output:  ${output}

    Should Not Be Empty             ${output}
    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${output}        SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...              command=grep "${pattern}" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
    ...              host=${HOST_EPCSIM}

    Dated log       === check res answer ===
    Dated log       res answer:  ${output}
    ${passed}    ${info}      Run Keyword And Ignore Error       Should Contain X Times    ${output}    ${pattern}    2
    Dated log       dbg1 passed : ${passed}
    ${subCheckmilisec_shouldnotmatch}=    Run keyword if    '${passed}'=='PASS'     Run Keyword And Return Status    subCheckmilisec
    ...                           ELSE                    Should Contain X Times    ${output}    ${pattern}    1

    #on 2640            the 2 first Scell need to NOT be activated in the same millisecond
    #on 8533AB401 step2 the 2 first Scell need to be activated in the same millisecond
    #
    # summary chart
    #+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
    # Cases            i                       :    2640   : 8533AB401 :
    #+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
    # The 2 Scell are not in the same millisec :    good   : not good  :
    # The 2 Scell are     in the same millisec :  not good :   good    :
    #+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
    #=> we need to FAIL not good cases

    #!= none => samemilisecond /    #== none => 2640
    Run Keyword If    '${subCheckmilisec_shouldnotmatch}' == '${true}' and '${samemilisecond}'!='${none}'    FAIL    subCheckmilisec
    ...    ELSE IF    '${subCheckmilisec_shouldnotmatch}' == '${false}' and '${samemilisecond}'=='${none}'    FAIL    subCheckmilisec

subCheckmilisec
    [Documentation]   sub KW of Check_activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs
    ...               return  true if NOT in the same millisec
    ${output}    SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...          command=grep "activated successfully at airphone" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log | awk -F " " '{print $2}'
    ...          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}
    Dated log     grep result:  ${output}
    ${first}=     Get Line      ${output}    0
    ${second}=    Get Line      ${output}    1
    ${rest}    ${lastf} =       Split String From Right    ${first}     .    1
    ${rest}    ${lasts} =       Split String From Right    ${second}    .    1
    ${shouldnotmatch}=          Run Keyword And Return Status    Should Not Match            ${lastf}    ${lasts}
    return    ${shouldnotmatch}

subCheckmilisec_V2
    [Documentation]   sub KW of Check_activated_successfully_at_airphone_onegateLogs
    ...               return  boolean sos_match according arguments
    ...
    ...               in ${output} we will find only grep result like below from egate_console.log
    ...               15:20:25.944 15:20:25.944 INF: UEC-1: L2: <DL CHANNEL> [UeId:2,SubcellId:33] SCellIndex 1 activated successfully at airphone.
    ...               15:20:25.944 15:20:25.944 INF: UEC-1: L2: <DL CHANNEL> [UeId:2,SubcellId:32] SCellIndex 2 activated successfully at airphone.
    [Arguments]    ${samemilisecond}=${none}    ${between_occ}=1-2    ${deviation}=0
    Dated log   subCheckmilisec_V2 arguments: >${samemilisecond}<>${between_occ}<>${deviation}<

    ${output}    SSH Wait For Connect and Cmd
    ...          command=grep "activated successfully at airphone" ${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log | awk -F " " '{print $2}'
    ...          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}


    Dated log     grep result:  ${output}

    # modif pour ajout deviation
#    ${lastf}    Set Variable    1111
#    ${lasts}    Set Variable    2222
#    ${lastt}    Set Variable    3333

    ${first}=     Get Line      ${output}    0     #collect in a variable of the first occurency
    ${second}=    Get Line      ${output}    1     #    "                        second  "
    ${third}=     Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='2-3'    Get Line      ${output}    2


    # modif pour ajout deviation
    ${diff12}=       Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='1-2'    Subtract Time From Time    ${second}    ${first}
    ...                          ELSE    Set Variable    2222
    ${diff23}=       Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='2-3'    Subtract Time From Time    ${third}    ${second}
    ...                          ELSE    Set Variable    3333
#work in the variable to kept only the millisec part of each occurency
#    ${rest}    ${lastf} =       Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='1-2'    Split String From Right    ${first}     .    1
#    ${rest}    ${lasts} =       Split String From Right    ${second}    .    1
#    ${rest}    ${lastt} =       Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='2-3'    Split String From Right    ${third}     .    1

    #DOD
    Dated log  first ${first} second ${second} third(ifany) ${third}
    Dated log  diff12 ${diff12} diff23(ifany) ${diff23}
#    Dated log  first ${lastf} second ${lasts} third(ifany) ${lastt}

    # Modif pour ajout deviation
    Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='1-2'and'${samemilisecond}'=='samemilisecond'and'${deviation}'<'${diff12}'
    ...                                                                       Fail    1-2 are not in the same millisec
    ...    ELSE IF    '${between_occ}'=='2-3'and'${samemilisecond}'=='NOTsamemilisecond'and'${diff23}'<'${deviation}'
    ...                                                                       Fail    2-3 are in the same millisec
#    Run Keyword If    '${between_occ}'=='1-2'and'${samemilisecond}'=='samemilisecond'and'${lastf}'!='${lasts}'
#    ...                                                                       Fail    1-2 are not in the same millisec
#    ...    ELSE IF    '${between_occ}'=='2-3'and'${samemilisecond}'=='samemilisecond'and'${lasts}'=='${lastt}'
#    ...                                                                       Fail    2-3 are in the same millisec

Check_sCellToAddModList_onegateLogs
    [Documentation]    Check sCellToAddModList on egate console Logs

    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    Grep and check in file          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}             file=${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
    ...                             grep=sCellToAddModList          pattern=sCellToAddModList

Check_sCellIndex_onegateLogs
    [Documentation]   Check sCellIndex and targeted physCellId messages in egate console log :
    ...
    ...                     sCellToAddModList
    ...                     {
    ...                       {
    ...                         sCellIndex 1,   <<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<
    ...                         sCellConfigCommon
    ...                         {
    ...                           physCellId 50, <<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<
    ...
    ...     and so one ...
    ...
    ...            DOD  need to find physCell id 51 & 50 (order not important)
    ...            sCellIndex 1 or 2 (combination not important)
    ...
    ...            &{NrRel_TargetedbyWeight_List}    NRCELL-1=50    NRCELL-2=51
    ...
    ...            actdeact is an aoptional arg to check if sCellIndex is activated or deactivated
    [Arguments]    ${ScellEngaged}    ${actdeact}=${None}

    DdatedLog  Arguments 1: ${ScellEngaged}
    DdatedLog  Arguments 2: ${actdeact}
    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${count}=    Set Variable    ${0}
    FOR     ${idx}                          IN                              @{ScellEngaged}
            DdatedLog   idx : ${idx}
            ${count}=                     Evaluate                        ${count} + ${1}
            ${phyid}=                     Get From Dictionary             ${ScellEngaged}    ${idx}
            Run Keyword If                '${actdeact}'=='${None}'
            ...                           Grep and check in file          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}             file=${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
            ...                           grep=sCellIndex                 pattern=sCellIndex ${count}
            ...  ELSE
            ...                           Grep and check in file          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}             file=${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
            ...                           grep=SCellIndex                 pattern=SCellIndex ${count} ${actdeact}   #attention SC... uppercase
            Run Keyword If                '${actdeact}'=='${None}'             #this part is played only if only one parameter is present
            ...                           Grep and check in file          host=${HOST_EPCSIM}             file=${tl.core.dir_path}/egate_console.log
            ...                           grep=physCellId                 pattern=physCellId ${phyid}
    END

Cqi_Param
    [Documentation]    DO NOT USED ANYMORE set cqi PARAMETER FOR  EACH ue on the 2 cell
    ...                see dictionary definition above
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    Dated log  Arguments 1: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    FOR    ${ue_desc}    IN      @{ue_list_de_dico}
            ${ueid}=         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    ue
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} CQI settings
            wtsemu.ue_cqi_param    id=${ueid}    scell=0    on=nr    nr_ri_mode=fixed    nr_ri=1
            wtsemu.ue_cqi_param    id=${ueid}    scell=1    on=nr    nr_ri_mode=fixed    nr_ri=1
    END

Traffic
    [Documentation]    * Start DL traffic for this TC
    ...                see dictionary definition above
    ...                * Traffic is done according above param.TrafficDuration
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}    ${step}=${EMPTY}

    #Cqi_Param    ${ue_list_de_dico}   #Not used anymore
    DdatedLog  Arguments 1: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    FOR    ${ue_desc}                                        IN                     @{ue_list_de_dico}              #@{Dico_ue_list}
            ${ueid}=                                         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    ue                   #ue
            ${trf_id}=                                       Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    trf_id
            ${TptDL}=                                        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    traffDL${step}
            ${TptUL}=                                        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    traffUL${step}
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic to ${TptDL} Mbps DL
            trfdl  ue=${ueid}    pdu=${ueid}    qfi=1    mbps=${TptDL}
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic to ${TptUL} Mbps UL
            wtsemu.trf_data_start      ue=${ueid}    pdu=${ueid}    qfi=1    dir=ul
            ...                        trf_id=${trf_id}    mbps=${TptUL}
    END

trfdl
    [Documentation]    As loop in loop is not possible in Robot this is
    ...                a sub KW of Traffic KW in charge to start traffic
    ...                Huge traffic is possible up to  3500 Mbps In DL :
    ...                175 Mbps maximum is possible by trf_id, egate limit to 20 Trf_id, Maximum traffic rate
    ...                is so theoricaly 175 (max Mbps by trf_id) x nb max trf_id (20) 3500 Mbps on DL
    [Arguments]    ${ue}=1    ${pdu}=1    ${qfi}=1    ${mbps}=22

    Dated log   Args_trf: ue ${ue} pdu ${pdu} qfi ${qfi} mbps ${mbps}
    ${trfid}     set variable    1
    FOR    ${i}    IN RANGE    9999999
            # Dated log  mbps ${mbps}
            Dated log  trf_id ${trfid}
            ${complement}          Evaluate                ${mbps} - 175    #175 is the maximum DL TP by trf_id
            #Dated log  complement ${complement}
            Run Keyword If         ${complement}>0 and ${mbps}>=175
                ...                                        wtsemu.trf_data_start       ue=${ue}    pdu=${pdu}    qfi=${qfi}    dir=dl
                ...                                                                    trf_id=${trfid}    mbps=175
                ...     ELSE IF    ${mbps}>0 and ${mbps}<=175
                ...                                        wtsemu.trf_data_start       ue=${ue}    pdu=${pdu}    qfi=${qfi}    dir=dl
                ...                                                                    trf_id=${trfid}    mbps=${mbps}
                ...     ELSE                               Exit For Loop
            ${mbps}     set variable    ${complement}
            ${trfid}   Evaluate        ${trfid} + 1
            Run Keyword If    ${trfid} > 19    Exit For Loop       #Trf_id max = 20
            sleep   2s   #to no let start traffic too quickly
    END

trf_stop_DL
    [Documentation]    * Stop DL traffic for all ue in ${ue_list_de_dico} list
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    DdatedLog  Argument 1 TS dl: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    FOR    ${ue_desc}    IN      @{ue_list_de_dico}
            ${ueid}=         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      ue
            wtsemu.trf_data_stop    ue=${ueid}    pdu=${ueid}    qfi=1    dir=dl
    END

trf_stop_UL
    [Documentation]    * Stop UL traffic for all ue in ${ue_list_de_dico} list
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    FOR    ${ue_desc}    IN      @{ue_list_de_dico}

        ${ueid}=         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      ue
        wtsemu.trf_data_stop    ue=${ueid}    pdu=${ueid}    dir=ul
    END

Traffics Check
    [Documentation]    This KW check for each TP if Average traffic
    ...                is on ${deviation_in_percent} range 50% as default value
    ...                for all ue in the list ${ue_list_de_dico}
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}  ${deviation_in_percent}=50

    DdatedLog  Arguments 1: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    DdatedLog  Arguments 2: ${deviation_in_percent}

    Dated log  Traffic_Check with ${deviation_in_percent} deviation possible

    FOR    ${ue_desc}        IN      @{ue_list_de_dico}
            ${ueid}=         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      ue
            ${trf_id}=       Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      trf_id
            ${TptDL}=        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      traffDL
            ${TptUL}=        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}      traffUL

            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid}  traffic check with ${TptDL} Mbps DL
            DOD  ue=${ueid}  pdu=${ueid}  qfi=1  trf_id=${trf_id}  dir=dl  expected_data_rate=${TptDL}  deviation_in_percent=${deviation_in_percent}
            DOD  ue=${ueid}  pdu=${ueid}  qfi=1  trf_id=${trf_id}  dir=ul  expected_data_rate=${TptUL}  deviation_in_percent=${deviation_in_percent}
    END

DOD
    [Documentation]    This is the DOD Traffic check mechanisum foe 1 ue
    ...                is on ${deviation_in_percent} range 5% as default value
    [Arguments]    ${ue}=1    ${pdu}=1    ${qfi}=1    ${trf_id}=1    ${dir}=dl
    ...            ${expected_data_rate}=5    ${deviation_in_percent}=5

    Dated log  Arg: ue:${ue} pdu:${pdu} qfi:${qfi} tref_id:${trf_id} dir:${dir} expected:${expected_data_rate} deviation:${deviation_in_percent}

    wtsemu.bearer_stats_clear       ue=${ue}    pdu=${pdu}    qfi=${qfi}    dir=bi            #bi is Ul and Dl

    #${average_out}=    UteWts.Get Average Traffic Rate    ue=${ue}    pdu=${pdu}    qfi=${qfi}    trf_id=${trf_id}    dir=${dir}
    sleep   15s    #to let Berear_stat buffer collect again
    wtsemu.Bearer Stats             ue=${ue}
    ...                             dir=${dir}                        #trf_id=${trf_id}
    ...                             qfi=${qfi}                        pdu=${pdu}

    CallSetup.Flush Egate Console Buffer
    Traced sleep   3s  msg=wait 3s to flush egate memory on egate_console.log
    ${status}    ${output}     Run Keyword And Ignore Error            wtsemu.read_wtsemu_output_until
    ...                        expected=Average packet interval        timeout=20
    ${output}=                 Get Lines Containing String             ${output}          Average data rate
    ${output}=                 Replace String      ${output}      Average data rate       ${EMPTY}
    @{words}=                  Split String        ${output}      (
    ${average_out}=            Strip String        ${words[0]}
    should not be empty     ${average_out}
    Dated log  average_out: ${average_out}
    ${average}    Convert To Integer    ${average_out}
    ${MEGA}=    Set Variable      1000000
    ${average_rate}=    Evaluate      ${average} / ${MEGA}
    ## compare with expected data rate with percentage
    ${min}=             Evaluate                                ${expected_data_rate} * (100 - ${deviation_in_percent}) / 100
    ${max}=             Evaluate                                ${expected_data_rate} * (100 + ${deviation_in_percent}) / 100
    ${statusError}=     Evaluate                                ${min} <= ${average_rate}
    ${statusWarn}=      Evaluate                                ${average_rate} <= ${max}
    ${statusStr}        Set variable if                         '${statusError}'=='True'
    ...                 REACHED                                 NOT REACHED
    ${statusStr}        Set variable if                         '${statusWarn}'=='True'
    ...                 ${statusStr}                            EXCEEDED
    Dated Log           Average data rate in ${dir} trf_id=${trf_id} for ${statusStr}: expected = ${expected_data_rate}, current = ${average_rate}
    Run Keyword If      '${statusError}'!='True'                 Fail    Data rate failure
    [Return]    ${statusStr}

Traffics Stop
    [Documentation]    * Stop DL & UL  (used on normal way and in Teardown)
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}    ${dir}=both

    Dated log  Arguments 1: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    Dated log  Arguments 2: ${dir}
    Run keyword if    '${dir}'=='both' or '${dir}'=='dl'     trf_stop_DL   ${ue_list_de_dico}
    ...               ELSE                                   trf_stop_UL   ${ue_list_de_dico}

    ${TRF_ongoing}=    Set Variable If   ${TRF_ongoing} == ${True}    ${False}    ${True}  #astuce set to Dalse and not none see Builtin
    Dated log  TRAFFIC STOPPED TRF_ongoing set to ${TRF_ongoing}


# - - - VONR CORNER - - -
Add_VONR_PDU
    [Documentation]    Add VONR bearers (QFI:2 fiveQI:5 and QFI:3 fiveQI:1)
    ...                see dictionary definition above
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    DdatedLog  Arguments 1: ${ue_list_de_dico}
    FOR    ${ue_desc}                                           IN                      @{ue_list_de_dico}
            ${ueid}=                                            Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    ue
            Dated log                                           id ${ueid} PDU session modify adding FIVEQi-5 BEARER
            CallSetup.UE PDU Session Modify                     ue=${ueid}  pdu=${ueid}  qfta=2  by=amf
            Dated log                                           id ${ueid} PDU session modify adding FIVEQi-1 BEARER
            sleep                                               1s
            CallSetup.UE PDU Session Modify                     ue=${ueid}  pdu=${ueid}  qfta=3  by=amf
    END
    sleep   2s
Traffic_VONR
    [Documentation]    * Start DL and UL traffic for this TC
    ...                * Traffic DL/UL are on 3 bearers
    ...                * As 175 Mbps maximum is possible by trf_id, this TC is able to complete on a second trf_id
    ...                Maximum traffic rate is so 350 Mbps on DL
    ...                * Traffic is INFINITE
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    Dated log  dicogeneral ${ue_list_de_dico}
    FOR    ${ue_desc}                                        IN                        @{ue_list_de_dico}              #@{Dico_ue_list}
            ${ueid}=                                         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    ue                   #ue
            ${TptDL}=                                        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    traffDL
            ${TptUL}=                                        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    traffUL

            ${complement}           Evaluate             ${TptDL} - 175
            Fill UE Property    ${ueid}
            Dated log  UE_profiles_list ${UE_profiles_list}
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic to ${TptDL} Mbps DL on FIVEQi-6 BEAER
            Run Keyword If   ${TptDL} <= 175
            ...              Traffic.Traffic UE DL    ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[0]    throughput=${TptDL}
            ...                                 maxThroughputPerTransfer=300        shouldBeStop=False     shouldBeCheck=False
            ...                                 duration=1s
            ...     ELSE     Run Keywords
            ...              Dated log        Traffic need more than more 175 Mbps so need on second trf_id ${complement} Mbps              AND
            ...              Traffic.Traffic UE DL    ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[0]    throughput=175
            ...                                 maxThroughputPerTransfer=300        shouldBeStop=False     shouldBeCheck=False
            ...                                 duration=1s                                                                                 AND
            ...              Traffic.Traffic UE DL    ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[2]    throughput=${complement}
            ...                                 maxThroughputPerTransfer=300        shouldBeStop=False     shouldBeCheck=False
            ...                                 duration=1s
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic TCP DL on FIVEQi-5 BEARER
            ${UE_profiles_list[4].throughput}   Set Variable                                    ${None}
            Traffic.Traffic UE DL               ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[4]                protocol=tcp
            ...                                 shouldBeCheck=False   shouldBeStop=False     duration=1s
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic amr_wb_18_25 DL on FIVEQi-1 BEARER
            ${UE_profiles_list[6].throughput}   Set Variable                                    ${None}
            Traffic.Traffic UE DL               ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[6]                rtp_codec=amr_wb_18_25
            ...                                 shouldBeCheck=False   shouldBeStop=False     duration=1s
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic to ${TptUL} Mbps UL
            Traffic.Traffic UE UL    ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[1]    throughput=${TptUL}
            ...                                 maxThroughputPerTransfer=300        shouldBeStop=False     shouldBeCheck=False
            ...                                 duration=1s
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic TCP UL on FIVEQi-5 BEARER
            Traffic.Traffic UE UL               ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[5]                protocol=tcp
            ...                                 shouldBeCheck=False   shouldBeStop=False     duration=1s
            Dated log  Ue_id ${ueid} start traffic amr_wb_18_25 UL on FIVEQi-1 BEARER
            ${UE_profiles_list[7].throughput}   Set Variable                                    ${None}
            Traffic.Traffic UE UL               ueSetting=${UE_profiles_list}[7]                rtp_codec=amr_wb_18_25
            ...                                 shouldBeCheck=False   shouldBeStop=False     duration=1s
            ${TRF_ongoing}=    Set Variable If   ${TRF_ongoing} == ${False}    ${True}    ${False}
            Dated log  TRF_ongoing?: ${TRF_ongoing}
    END
Check_DL_Trafic_VONR
    [Documentation]    see documentation in Keywords TC 2640-AB_08 SA
    ...                For calcualting the PM values for Traffic in Defaut bearer
    ...                You can use the EXEL file \\eseefsn50.emea.nsn-net.net\rotta4internal\5G_3\paris-saclay\FEATURE_2640\CALCUL_TPUT_2640.xlsx

    Dated Log   Pause 10 mn to get the next PM period
    sleep   600s
    Dated Log   Pause ended
    IBCA Collect PM Counters File
    # Check LEAGACY RLC Counters
    Dated Log   Check Legacy Counters for QOS1, 5 and 6
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_In_A_Range    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_QOS1}    720    722
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_In_A_Range    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_QOS5}    617    619
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_In_A_Range    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_QOS6}    11192000    11305000    #300 0.5% #301Mbps 11235000    11348000
    # Check RLC Counters for CA primary path and secondary path
    Dated Log   Check Primary+secondary Path Counters for QOS1
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_Expected_Value    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_primary_QOS1}    0
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_Expected_Value    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_secondary_QOS1}    0
    Dated Log   Check Primary+secondary Path Counters for QOS5
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_Sum_eqal    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_primary_QOS5}
    ...                                                     ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_secondary_QOS5}
    ...                                                     ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_QOS5}
    Dated Log   Check Primary+secondary Path Counters for QOS6
    5GC002640_PMCounterCheck_Sum_eqal    ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_primary_QOS6}
    ...                                                     ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_secondary_QOS6}
    ...                                                     ${PM_Counter_DL_RLC_PDU_volume_QOS6}

Traffics VONR Stop
    [Documentation]    Stop Traffic DL & UL for 3 bearers VONR
    ...                and detach UE
    [Arguments]    ${ue_list_de_dico}

    FOR    ${ue_desc}                                        IN                        @{ue_list_de_dico}
            ${ueid}=                                         Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    ue
            ${TptDL}=                                        Get From Dictionary    ${ue_desc}    traffDL

            Fill UE Property    ${ueid}
            @{DL_UE_profiles_list}    Create List    ${UE_profiles_list}[0]  ${UE_profiles_list}[4]   ${UE_profiles_list}[6]
            run keyword IF     '${TptDL}' > '175'     APPEND TO LIST     ${DL_UE_profiles_list}     ${UE_profiles_list}[2]

            Traffic.Traffic Stop UEs    ${DL_UE_profiles_list}    dir=dl
            @{UL_UE_profiles_list}    Create List    ${UE_profiles_list}[1]  ${UE_profiles_list}[5]   ${UE_profiles_list}[7]

            Traffic.Traffic Stop UEs    ${UL_UE_profiles_list}    dir=ul

            sleep   1s
            CallSetup.UE Deregister     id=${ueid}
    END
    ${TRF_ongoing}=    Set Variable     ${False}
    Dated log  TRAFFIC STOPPED TRF_ongoing set to ${TRF_ongoing}

#****************************** Keywords for capture traces***************************************
Start Mirroring And Traces gNB
    [Documentation]      Start Mirroring (present for debug purpose)

    ${capture_gnb_x2}      Capture CORE Set Upon Config
    ${capture_gnb_l1l2}    Capture L1L2 Set Upon Config
    ${capture_gnb_l3l2}    Capture CPRT Set Upon Config

    # ADT - add filter for capture_gnb_x2
    ${filter F1AP}                  Get Filter For F1AP                     ${capture_gnb_x2}
    ${filter X2AP}                  Get Filter For X2AP                     ${capture_gnb_x2}
    ${capture_gnb_x2.filter}        set variable                            ${filter F1AP} or ${filter X2AP}

    # ${capture_gnb_l3l2.filter}       Get Filter To Exclude protocols    capture=${capture_gnb_l3l2}    protocolList=${filter_protocol}

    ${capture_gnb_l3l2.filter}       Get Filter To Exclude protocols    capture=${capture_gnb_l3l2}    protocolList=${filter_protocol}
    ${capture_gnb_l1l2.filter}       Get Filter To Exclude protocols    capture=${capture_gnb_l1l2}    protocolList=${filter_protocol}

    Capture Init         ${capture_gnb_x2}        suffix=_X2_backhaul
    Capture Init         ${capture_gnb_l1l2}      suffix=_filter_protocol
    Capture Init         ${capture_gnb_l3l2}      suffix=_L3L2_filter_protocol

    Set Suite Variable    ${capture_gnb_x2}
    Set Suite Variable    ${capture_gnb_l1l2}
    Set Suite Variable    ${capture_gnb_l3l2}
    Dated Log    -----> Starting capture X2 in gNB.\n
    Capture Start         ${capture_gnb_x2}
    Dated Log    -----> Starting capture L2L1 in gNB.\n
    Capture Start         ${capture_gnb_l1l2}
    Dated Log    -----> Starting capture L3L2 in gNB.\n
    Capture Start         ${capture_gnb_l3l2}

Stop Mirroring And Traces gNB
    [Documentation]      Stop Mirroring (present for debug purpose)

    Dated Log    [Stopping Mirroring And Traces gNB]
    Capture Stop    ${capture_gnb_l1l2}
    Dated Log    -----> Traces L2L1 saved under ${capture_gnb_l1l2.path}\n
    Capture Stop    ${capture_gnb_x2}
    Dated Log    -----> Traces X2 saved under ${capture_gnb_x2.path}\n
    Capture Stop    ${capture_gnb_l3l2}
    Dated Log    -----> Traces L2L3 saved under ${capture_gnb_l3l2.path}\n

Start Mirroring And Traces AP
    [Documentation]      Start Mirroring (present for debug purpose)

    Dated Log    [Starting Mirroring And Traces Airphone]
    ${capture_ap_l1l2}    Capture L1L2 Set Upon Config    ${AP_DU}
    ${capture_ap_l1l2.filter}      Get Filter To Exclude protocols   capture=${capture_ap_l1l2}
    ...                                                              protocolList=${filter_protocol}
    Capture Init         ${capture_ap_l1l2}     suffix=_filter_protocol
    Set Suite Variable    ${capture_ap_l1l2}
